/-
  Global existence for the bridge, split-chain form (memory-bounded).

  For each component F_i: at any y ∈ ℝ³ with K(y) ≠ 0, every root ξ of
  the fiber cubic, with b, c the shape-relation values, satisfies
  F_i(ξ, b, c) = y_i.  Proved in three steps per component — eliminate c
  (exL1_i, cofactor = the c-coefficient of F_i), eliminate b
  (exL2_i, division cofactor E), then the pure quotient identity
  (exL3_i) — so no single ring check holds the full six-variable
  product.  Assembly: exists_glob1/2/3.
-/
